# What `docker build -f api/Dockerfile .` must NOT upload as build context
# (api/cloudbuild.yaml builds with the repo ROOT as the context; the app build
# has its own list in app/.dockerignore, whose context is `app`).
#
# `**/` on every generated directory, and it is not decoration. A .dockerignore
# pattern without a separator is matched against the path RELATIVE TO THE
# CONTEXT ROOT — Go's filepath.Match, not gitignore semantics — so a bare
# `node_modules` covers only a top-level one. There is none; the 451 MB sit in
# `app/node_modules`, and they travelled with every API build. Same for the
# 216 `__pycache__` directories, `app/dist`, and — the largest of them — the
# InkSight venv and weights under `tools/`, which come to 3.4 GB on a machine
# that has run route B. Measured on 2026-09-04: 339 MiB of context before,
# 44 MiB after, in a checkout WITHOUT those weights.
#
# `.gcloudignore` next to this file needs no such treatment: it uses gitignore
# semantics, where a bare name already matches at any depth.

.git
.gitignore
**/.idea
**/.vscode
.serena
.claude

# Python: environments, bytecode and tool caches, at any depth.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# JS: installed and generated by the app build, which does not run here.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage

# The InkSight route's local half: a 3.4 GB venv + checkpoint tree that is
# gitignored, so a CI clone never has it — but a local `docker build` does.
tools/inksight/weights
tools/inksight/out

# `.env*`, not the three names that happen to exist: .env holds DATABASE_URL
# and ADMIN_TOKEN, and a variant nobody thought of (.env.staging) fell straight
# through the old list into the build context. Same rule in .gcloudignore and
# app/.dockerignore.
**/.env*

# Not shipped by api/Dockerfile: it copies api/, core/, alembic/, data/sources/,
# app/prerender/ and one JSON out of tools/.
docs
tests
.github
MEMORY.md
